===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[chromium|Chromium]], when used to plate other metals.
# {{lb|en|computing|graphical user interface}} The basic [[structural]] [[element]]s used in a [[graphical user interface]], such as window frames and [[scroll bar]]s, as opposed to the content.
#* {{cite-web|last=Nielsen|first=Jakob|date=2012-01-29|url=https://www.nngroup.com/articles/browser-and-gui-chrome/|title=Browser and GUI Chrome|work=Nielsen Norman Group homepage|publisher=Nielsen Norman Group|accessdate=2019-09-24}}
#*: “Similarly [to the chrome exterior of an automobile], in most modern GUIs, the '''chrome''' lives around the edges of the screen, surrounding the middle area, which is dedicated to the user's data.”
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2020-01-04|quotee=Maf Vosburgh|author=Jimmy Grewal|title=Internet Explorer 5 for Mac: twentieth anniversary|work=Jimmy's Blog|url=http://jimmy.grew.al/macie5-twentieth-anniversary/}}
#*: {{quote|en|I had the idea of making our browser '''chrome''' match the actual hardware you were on. If your Mac’s bezel was Bondi blue, we’d make our UI Bondi blue.}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} [[handgun]]s (collectively)

